<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Delium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">424 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Delium was fought in 424 BCE near Delium on the Boeotian coast during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>. The Boeotian army under the Theban commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagondas">Pagondas</a>, drawn up 25 ranks deep and supported by a surprise cavalry attack, defeated an Athenian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hippocrates">Hippocrates</a>, who was killed. The philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socrates">Socrates</a> fought on the Athenian side, and the battle ended Athenian plans to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-delium.jpg" alt="Battle of Delium" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Couture · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socrates_at_the_Battle_of_Delium_(Thomas_Couture,_1843).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
